cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Mutation Score Understates Oracle Provenance: Agent-Generated Test
  Suites on Defects4J, With and Without the Implementation
message: >-
  If you use this data or these scripts, please cite the repository.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Parpal
    given-names: Sergi
repository-code: https://github.com/sergiparpal/mutation-study
abstract: >-
  Two test suites were generated per Defects4J bug with the same agent and
  model, under two conditions: the agent either works in the project's source
  tree or sees only its javadoc. The comparison was run twice on the same 40
  bugs. In the second campaign, with the benchmark's metadata removed from
  the working copy, the conditions enforced by a sandbox, every transcript
  kept and the analysis fixed in advance, real-fault detection falls from 56%
  to 18% over 39 bugs, while mutation score falls from 54% to 39% and line
  coverage from 84% to 70%. The first campaign, on standard Defects4J
  checkouts, gave 72% against 14%. The repository holds the generation and
  measurement scripts, the protocol and full record of the second campaign,
  the per-suite measurements, an EvoSuite baseline, a hand classification of
  the 40 faults, a probe of what the model recalls about each fault with no
  code in context, two post-cutoff replication corpora, and an audit of what
  the benchmark's own files told the agent.
keywords:
  - test generation
  - mutation testing
  - Defects4J
  - large language models
  - empirical software engineering
license: MIT
license-url: https://github.com/sergiparpal/mutation-study/blob/main/LICENSE
date-released: 2026-10-01
